    "text": "<math><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Bulky base is present, it will abstract proton, hence will undergo E2 reaction<br ><img src=\"assets\\st0009_abea9e2cd50d.jpeg\"/><br ><math><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Hydrogen ion will protonate the oxygen of methoxy group and make it a good leaving group, hence methanol and t-butyl bromide is formed.<br ><img src=\"assets\\st0009_903c58f2a530.jpeg\"/><br ><math><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Methoxy group will abstract proton. E2 elimination occur<br ><img src=\"assets\\st0009_1206f498c86b.jpeg\"/><br ><math><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></math> It will undergo <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math> mechanism.<br ><img src=\"assets\\st0009_54b29b3e56f5.jpeg\"/>"
